From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teng Fan <tengf@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] groff: disable parallel make for native build

groff-native 1.24.1 can fail intermittently while generating
doc/automake.pdf because preconv has not been built before test-groff
attempts to execute it.

The failure is caused by incomplete build dependencies exposed during
parallel compilation:

  groff: error: couldn't exec preconv: No such file or directory

Disable parallel make for groff-native as a workaround until the
upstream build dependency issue is resolved.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [workaround for parallel build race]

Signed-off-by: Teng Fan <tengf@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 meta/recipes-extended/groff/groff_1.24.1.bb | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/meta/recipes-extended/groff/groff_1.24.1.bb b/meta/recipes-extended/groff/groff_1.24.1.bb
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/meta/recipes-extended/groff/groff_1.24.1.bb
+++ b/meta/recipes-extended/groff/groff_1.24.1.bb
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+# Work around missing build dependencies exposed by parallel compilation.
+# The issue affects groff-native while generating documentation.
+PARALLEL_MAKE:class-native = "-j1"
+
 SUMMARY = "GNU troff text-formatting system"
 DESCRIPTION = "The groff package contains programs for processing and \
 formatting text and images."
-- 
